# dp - SSH rescue keys, seeded by launch_chffrplus.sh::seed_ssh_keys().
#
# Why this file exists: the car only accepts publickey logins, and the keys it
# trusts come from the /data/params/d/GithubSshKeys param. A reinstall wipes
# /data, so that param disappears together with everything else. If the install
# then fails and the UI is stuck on the comma logo, there is no way to enter a
# GitHub username either - the box is unreachable over the network and the only
# way back in is a physical reflash.
#
# seed_ssh_keys() copies this file into /data/params/d/GithubSshKeys before
# build.py runs, so SSH stays available no matter how far the install got. It
# never overwrites an existing param, so a username entered from the UI wins.
#
# PUBLIC KEYS ONLY. The matching private key (id_ed25519, the file without the
# .pub suffix) must never be committed here - this repository is source, and
# anyone holding that private key can log into the device.
#
# To let another machine in: generate a keypair there and append its .pub line.
